{
  "id": "adult-attachment-interview",
  "term": "Adult Attachment Interview",
  "definition": "The Adult Attachment Interview is a research interview used in developmental attachment work to assess an adult’s attachment representation, especially how early attachment experiences are processed and expressed. It focuses mainly on unconscious aspects of attachment and examines them through the person’s spoken account, including signs of defensiveness or idealization.",
